sentences.text:
The petitioner is directed to be enlarged on bail in Spl.C.C.No.1497/2024 pending before the Court of Addl. City Civil and Sessions Judge, FTSC-IV Bengaluru, arising out of Crime No.203/2024 registered by Ashoknagar Police Station, Bengaluru City, for the offences punishable under Sections 3(1), 3(2B), 4 & 5 of Immoral Traffic Prevention Act, 1956, Sections 370(4),
376(2)(n), 376(3), 109 of IPC and Sections 4(2), 5(l), 6 & 16 of the Protection of Children from Sexual Offences Act, 2012, subject to the following conditions:
a) The petitioner shall execute personal bond for a sum of Rs.2,00,000/- (Rupees Two Lakh NC: 2025:KHC:19633 HC-KAR only) with two sureties out of which, one shall be local surety for the likesum to the satisfaction of the jurisdictional Court;
b) The petitioner shall appear regularly on all the dates of hearing before the Trial Court unless the Trial Court exempts her appearance for valid reasons;
Parimal Das vs State Of Karnataka on 10 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/163002406/
4 c) The petitioner shall not directly or indirectly threaten or tamper with the prosecution witnesses;
 d) The petitioner shall not involve in  similar offences in future;
 e) The petitioner shall not leave the jurisdiction of the Trial Court without permission of the said Court until the case registered against her is disposed off.
SD/-
(S VISHWAJITH SHETTY) JUDGE VM Parimal Das vs State Of Karnataka on 10 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/163002406/
